CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
must never appear
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/11: a non-virtual constructor of a class template shall not
be implicitly instantiated unless odr-used.  The two-argument constructor here
is never used, so under lazy instantiation its assertion "must never appear"
does not enter the goto program and the forbidden pattern must be absent.  The
default constructor IS odr-used and is still instantiated (s.v is read).

This became CORE once the special members (constructors/destructors) were
deferred together with ordinary members and operators.  The destructor of a
*constructed* class is recovered from the type system ([class.dtor]/12) so
needed special members are still instantiated; see
doc/architectural/cpp-extern-template-member-instantiation.md §13.
